[[SECTION]]
MID: c9db1d330241f91938918b42824cefc3
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-ACCESS-POLICY-MIGRATION-adopt-existing-ci-identity-applications
TITLE: Adopt existing CI identity applications

[TEXT]
MID: b1ffe3c1afa96af2bdb273f2770bc111
STATEMENT: >>>
From the trusted VM session, run `codexiactl init --plan` or `codexiactl doctor`.
Confirm the repository and the certified public and management hostnames, and review the observed account, zone, Tunnel, Access applications and policy attachments.
With the fixed cf version, the read-only commands can report an incomplete observation when a Workers route or custom domain inventory requires a verified limited SDK credential.
Record that limitation and resolve any independent target, scope or policy conflict before proceeding.

Use `codexiactl init` for changes. Review each purpose, scope and expiry before approving temporary credential issuance, and review the resource diff before approving changes.
Keep each probe app's ID and AUD and the author-only parent.
Check that the exact-path Tunnel rules from `identity-probes.json` precede the catch-all and accept only each probe's AUD and the author AUD.
Check that the product Service Auth policy matches its exact repository and purpose tag and that the separate management app accepts only the two SSH tags for the selected repository.
Run the protected production preflight before changing an existing deployment and repeat it after the change.
For a VM that still uses the retired management path, establish an independently authorized way to close and verify publication before applying Cloudflare changes.
Preserve existing application and Tunnel IDs, audiences and valid credentials when the probe application still uses a shared policy selected by an explicit token ID, the protected host variables still identify the former management host, or public OAuth/MCP is already enabled.
These states require a rehearsed, owner-approved transition with the existing independent SSH connection and rollback evidence. Stop if the CLI cannot verify that transition. Keep each existing credential until the replacement passes its intended access check.

After an interrupted issuance or registration, retain the CLI checkpoint and repeat observation in the same trusted VM session and exclusive Settings window.
Compare the recorded repository, account, Environment and purpose against the Cloudflare inventory and the protected GitHub settings before retrying.
An existing issuance record with unknown registration or a missing one-time secret requires reconciliation before another credential can be requested.
Use the authorized account operation to determine whether the exact issuance was unused and may be retired. Verify expiry or retirement before replacing an ambiguous temporary credential.
Use a protected access check to confirm an existing GitHub Secret. Its name alone does not prove that the value was stored or can authenticate.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: 3a9a8cda203ddce1d64aa043f74b1e79
UID: DOC-DEPLOYMENT-ACCESS-POLICY-MIGRATION-gated-access-independent-oauth-and-mcp-paths
TITLE: Gated Access-independent OAuth and MCP paths

[TEXT]
MID: 5bb75d9a7d1cb22beccd0dd831d035fe
STATEMENT: >>>
Public OAuth and MCP paths require verified Passkey-first Better Auth runtime, a registered owner, limited MCP OAuth clients, API admission and remote MCP acceptance.
Before authorizing the exact-path transition, check the observed Bypass policies, Tunnel ingress and the product publication state.
The change stages the expected Tunnel routing before enabling the corresponding Bypass applications.

`public-protocol-paths.json` is the route allowlist. It includes only `/mcp`, the exact protected-resource and OAuth discovery metadata paths, JWKS, OAuth authorization/token/introspection/revocation/userinfo/consent endpoints, the login method and session reads, Passkey authentication options/verification, and fixed upstream OIDC sign-in/callback endpoints. The dedicated OAuth UI has exact Access paths for `/oauth/login`, `/oauth/consent`, and `/oauth/assets/*`; these static paths do not get Tunnel ingress entries. It does not include OAuth client registration, auth administration, Passkey management, project/data API routes, or wildcard `/api/auth/*`. The API continues to enforce OAuth token, session, scope, project and object authorization. Preserve the author application, the two CI identity applications and their AUDs. The catch-all Tunnel rule requires the author AUD.

Cloudflare documents that a more specific app path takes precedence without inheriting the hostname's parent policy, and that a Bypass/Everyone rule disables Access enforcement for that path. The OAuth login and consent pages use a dedicated Vite entry whose HTML and hashed assets stay under `/oauth/assets/*`. The Bypass entries cover only these two pages and that asset prefix; generic `/assets/*`, the Desktop UI route and all other static content stay behind the parent Access application. The retired `/mobile/` route has no Access exception or compatibility alias. Do not claim remote end-to-end OAuth acceptance from source review or metadata alone. See [Application paths](https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/access-controls/policies/app-paths/) and [Bypass a public endpoint](https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/access-controls/policies/common-policies/#bypass-a-public-endpoint).

The zone owner controls the shared WAF and rate-limit rules. If an interactive challenge affects an allowed protocol path, the zone rule owner must review a narrow method/path exception that preserves the rule's other predicates and all rate controls. Do not skip the whole hostname, `/api/*`, `/api/auth/*`, or all requests to a public route.

Require a reviewed diff limited to the named exact-path Access apps and the corresponding Tunnel ingress.
For rollback, verify that origin-side Access JWT validation is restored before removing the Bypass applications.
Source verification uses isolated fixtures and preserves the live deployment.

After a separately authorized edge change, run `pnpm verify:public-oauth-edge` with only `CODEXIA_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` set. This read-only probe sends no Access service token, cookie or bearer token. It checks the exact resource metadata audience and scope ceiling, OAuth/OIDC discovery and JWKS, the two required login reads, the dedicated login/consent HTML and every directly referenced `/oauth/assets/*` file, the expected `/mcp` 401 challenge, anonymous denial of `/api/projects`, and continued Access protection of `/desktop`. It does not complete an OAuth authorization code flow; use the disposable OAuth integration acceptance for that.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
